Third-party data redistributed in processed form

data/processed/ds-02-district-boundaries.geojson contains six administrative
polygons copied from geoBoundaries (www.geoboundaries.org), gbOpen release,
commit 9469f09, simplified geometries. Runfola D. et al. (2020) geoBoundaries:
A global database of political administrative boundaries. PLoS ONE 15(4):
e0231866. The per-country source licences are recorded in the gbOpen metadata
(Colombia: OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL; Ethiopia: Open Africa / Code for
Ethiopia, CC BY; Viet Nam: geoBoundaries / Wikipedia). The rainfall series
derived inside those polygons come from CHIRPS v2.0 (Climate Hazards Center,
UC Santa Barbara; Funk C. et al. 2015, Scientific Data 2:150066), read through
the IRI Data Library; CHIRPS is in the public domain.
